{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/907384-bizzare-crossover-question","id":907384,"title":"Bizzare Crossover question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-04T19:15:47-07:00","id":907384,"title":"Bizzare Crossover question","content":"Obviously, any changing breed PC will not match up to even the lowliest Exalted character, the games are built on different scales of power, nor even generally with a M:tA Mage (their free form powers are to open).<br /> <br /> But, IN YOUR OPINION, which changing breed (including Garou) is going to be BEST able to keep up with an Exalt and/or a Mage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T00:15:09-07:00","id":907499,"title":"","content":"In general, none of them have any advantages against the Exalted. It would all come down to individual builds more than specific Breeds.<br /> <br /> Fera vs. mages is largely a question of how well the Fera in question can catch a mage off guard. Mage's are incredibly powerful with preparation, but are easily going to go down if caught flatfooted.<br /> <br /> So, you need two major skillsets: Ambush attacks, and some magic stuff. High ranking Uktena Ragabash are a good baseline here, since Uktena Gifts give them access to a few useful magic-related Gifts, and Ragabash will get them access to sneaky powers, Umbra jump spam powers, and a few &quot;screw with enemy powers&quot; stuff. Properly built Bastet, Corax, Nagah, or Nuwisha can pull a lot of the same stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T08:44:48-07:00","id":907656,"title":"","content":"Let me clarify, the question is not about FIGHTING an exalt or mage, but rather in a mixed game where other players are playing an exalt and/or mage, which breed would be the most able to keep up with them, or I guess provide skills and abilities that are outside the Exalt and Mages purviews.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T12:26:29-07:00","id":907789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/907384-bizzare-crossover-question#post907384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obviously, any changing breed PC will not match up to even the lowliest Exalted character, the games are built on different scales of power, nor even generally with a M:tA Mage (their free form powers are to open).<br /> <br /> But, IN YOUR OPINION, which changing breed (including Garou) is going to be BEST able to keep up with an Exalt and/or a Mage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Which edition? Animal forms are going to be much, much more capable in 3e than in other editions. Even more so, if you rule that Mokole can turn into a tyrant lizard, using the 3e tyrant lizard stats.<br /> <br /> Assuming, of course, said Mokole didn't stack Tall and Behemoth until they started to resemble Godzilla, of course. That, too, could put them ahead, if the mechanics from W:tA weren't utterly horrid when it came to the hugest of the huge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T12:51:34-07:00","id":907807,"title":"","content":"Well run of the mill starting characters against run of the mill starting Terrestials could actually stand a chance if the Terrestrial wasn't combat heavy. But Rank 6 Shape Shifters are the types of individuals that could go toe to toe with a Dragon Blooded. A lot of Gifts go all of the place compared to Charms which builds off of established competency. So Dragonblooded or Starting Solars don't easily shrug off Tsunamis or Earthquakes. Rokea, Nagah, and Mokole are always useful in the Water.<br /> <br /> After all remember The Margrave Yuri Konietzko is the reincarnation of The Bull of the North Yurgen Kaneko.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T13:49:14-07:00","id":907846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TiwazTyrsfist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/907384-bizzare-crossover-question?p=907656#post907656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me clarify, the question is not about FIGHTING an exalt or mage, but rather in a mixed game where other players are playing an exalt and/or mage, which breed would be the most able to keep up with them, or I guess provide skills and abilities that are outside the Exalt and Mages purviews.</div> </div> </div> </div>For Exalted, it's up to the characters in question. There's very little that the Exalted as a whole don't have covered, so it would only be holes an individual group of them don't have covered<br /> <br /> For Mage, the details don't change much. Werewolves can move in and out of the Umbra with much greater ease, and require far less prep-time for maximum output. Mages are always best with time and preparation, while any of the Fera have the ability to go from 1 to 11 in either area of expertise virtually instantly. The balancing act there is mostly in that zone of the Mage being ready for X and the Fera being ready for not-X.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T03:36:27-07:00","id":963618,"title":"","content":"What kind of Exalt are we talking about here?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;There is a remedy for everything but death, a hope for everything but wickedness, and everything will lapse except righteousness.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6042-manusdomine","name":"ManusDomine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6042_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}